Mara,

Thank you. Taking your points in order, with one addition.

1. DSA (Saltmarren baseline data). The data-sharing agreement template is
   drafted. I will finalize it once Saltmarren's counsel confirms the
   retention clause; I have raised it with them and do not yet have a date.
   Until the DSA is signed, no student records leave Saltmarren. That
   includes the anonymized sample of transfer transcripts Delphine has
   offered to send you for the baseline. Anonymized or not, the
   transcript sample is a student record for this purpose, and it stays at
   Saltmarren until signature. In practical terms, the baseline part of your
   discovery is blocked on the unsigned DSA.

2. DPA (Scrivelo). The data processing agreement is on my list for next
   week. I will reply with a marked-up copy rather than a summary.

3. Process map. Delphine forwarded Rufus's process map this morning. For my
   purposes the step that matters is step 6, the course-by-course
   equivalency lookup: it is the bottleneck he identifies, and it is also the
   step where evaluators work directly from student records.

On timing: I note the site visit is on 2 March and the readout is targeted
for 19 March. Interviews with Saltmarren staff during the site visit do not
require the DSA, provided no records are copied or taken off campus. I am not
able to commit to a signature date ahead of the readout; that depends on
Saltmarren's counsel, and the agreement remains subject to their review.

Regards,
Agnieszka

